# Copy to .env.local (or .env) and adjust as needed. Vite only reads
# variables prefixed VITE_; a change requires restarting `npm run dev` (or
# rebuilding for production) to take effect.

# Timeout (ms) for scan-triggering requests: single-file scan, batch/ZIP/
# folder upload, GitHub repo scan, and live-editor scan. These can
# legitimately take minutes on a large real-world repo -- default is 20
# minutes. Bumped from 10 min after per-function inference
# (docs/PER_FUNCTION_INFERENCE_DESIGN.md) measured a real 200-file GitHub
# scan (curl) at 797.5s server-side, which already exceeded the old
# 10-minute default. This is a stopgap, not a real fix: the proper
# solution for very large repos is an async job (submit -> poll status ->
# fetch result) instead of one long blocking request. See README.md
# "Configuration".
VITE_SCAN_TIMEOUT_MS=1200000
